title: trash:prune
tags: [[GUI command]] Trash
kind: reference
summary: Trash: permanently delete the selected entry, or every entry (entry / all)

The GUI half of `mf trash prune`: what is pruned leaves the trash for good, its
bytes and its metarecords with it ([[Trash]]). `trash:prune entry` takes the
entry under the cursor of the [[trash panel]], `trash:prune all` every entry; each
asks for a confirmation first. Pruning by age or by size is command-line only
([[Trash retention]]).

Sending something ''to'' the trash is another command: deleting a file, from any
panel, puts it there.
